course: dictionary
lesson: 3370
title: Excuse: a reason, a pardon, or a polite phrase
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Excuse is one word with two jobs. As a noun, said ex-KYOOS, it is a reason you give to explain why you did something wrong or did not do something. As a verb, said ex-KYOOZ, it means to forgive someone for something small, or to let them not do a task. Check the sentence to see which job the word is doing.
explain: «Liking someone is never an excuse to hurt them.» Here excuse is a noun. Try swapping in reason: «Liking someone is never a reason to hurt them.» It still makes sense, so the meaning is right. Liking someone does not make hurting them acceptable.
explain: «Excuse me» is a polite phrase. You say it to get someone's attention, to ask someone to move, or to say sorry for a small thing. You can also use it before you leave the table: «May I be excused?»
explain: In the story, the birds make excuses: they find made-up reasons to hurry home. A made-up excuse is not the real reason. The good habit is to give a true reason, then take responsibility for what you did.
fact: Excuse (noun, said ex-KYOOS) means a reason given to explain a wrong or a missed task.
fact: Excuse (verb, said ex-KYOOZ) means to forgive someone for something small, or to let them not do something.
fact: «Excuse me» is a polite phrase to get attention, to ask someone to move, or to say sorry for a small thing.
fact: «May I be excused?» means may I leave the table.
fact: Making excuses means blaming other things instead of saying sorry, and «The dog ate my homework» is a famous example.
exercise: «Liking someone is never an excuse to hurt them.» What does excuse mean here? | A polite phrase to get attention | To forgive someone for a small thing | *A reason that would make it okay | A kind of bird
exercise: What is «Excuse me» used for? | To win a game | To tell a joke | *To get someone's attention politely | To say you are hungry
exercise: «...at once every bird finds an excuse to hurry home.» What does excuse mean here? | *A made-up reason | To forgive | A kind of bird | A polite phrase
test: In «May I be excused?», excuse is a verb meaning: | To be forgiven | To be polite | *To be let leave | A made-up reason
test: A note from a parent can excuse you from PE. What does excuse mean? | A made-up reason | A polite phrase | To hurry home | *To let you not do it
exam: Which is the correct way to say excuse as a noun? | ex-KOOS | ex-KYOOZ | *ex-KYOOS | ex-KYOOT
